  "body": "Follow-up of #3447.\n\n## What is missing\n\nThe setups now keep the order in which they were created. `SetupDef::order` holds the place (#3447). The user cannot change that order. There is no command and no MCP tool to move a setup up or down.\n\n## What to add\n\n- An undoable command, for example `ReorderSetup { name, position }`. It writes the new `order` values of the moved setup and of the setups between the two places. Undo writes the old values back.\n- The MCP tool for the command (for example `reorder_setup`), and its row in the `camcraft-mcp` skill.\n- A refusal when a setup would post before the setup that it takes its datum or carried stock from (`datum_from`, `stock_source: from_previous`).\n- Tests: the order after the command, after undo and after save and load, and in the posted program.\n\n## Done means\n\nA setup can be moved to a new place in the program through the command and through MCP. The move undoes. The post follows the new order.\n",
